{
  "$description": "How old Figma designs (D2 / Dash / D3 libraries, local components, hand-drawn layers) map to Lemonnade V3 (L3). Single source for scripts/figma/* (bundled in by scripts/figma/bundle.ts) and for docs/PLAYBOOK.md. Proven on the F&O file (2026-10-08/09): ~7.5k colours, ~1.1k numbers, ~1.6k texts, 300+ component swaps, 0 screens resized. Add a mapping here when you meet a new old name — never inside a one-off script.",
  "oldCollections": [
    "Dash → UI Colors",
    "Tokens",
    "Semantic tokens",
    "🎨 L3 Theme",
    "Base hex",
    "PrimitiveSize",
    "Spacing",
    "Border radius"
  ],
  "l3ColorPrefix": "🔷 L3/color/",
  "colors": {
    "$note": "old variable name → L3 theme token (without the '🔷 L3/color/' prefix). '#name' = decided by context (see contexts). Decisions: every D2 grey text/icon level collapses to content/secondary; text/brand keeps the exact lime (surface/accent/brand-default, not content/brand which renders olive). Names are matched after dropping the library prefix (D2/, D3/, Dash/) and '❌ [Discontinued] ', so 'color/text/secondary' and 'D2/color/text/secondary' are the same entry. A value can be an object {content, surface, border} when the right token depends on how the colour is used.",
